## 4. Improvement Prioritization Framework

### 4.1 Priority Matrix

| Impact | Effort | Priority |
|--------|--------|----------|
| High   | Low    | P0 (Critical) |
| High   | Medium | P1 (High) |
| High   | High   | P2 (Medium) |
| Medium | Low    | P1 (High) |
| Medium | Medium | P2 (Medium) |
| Medium | High   | P3 (Low) |
| Low    | Low    | P3 (Low) |
| Low    | Medium | P4 (Backlog) |
| Low    | High   | P4 (Backlog) |

### 4.2 Evaluation Criteria

Each improvement opportunity is scored (1-5) on:

1. **Impact on Performance:** Accuracy, speed, reliability
2. **Impact on Safety:** Risk reduction, error prevention
3. **Impact on Fairness:** Bias reduction, equity
4. **Impact on Compliance:** Regulatory adherence
5. **Impact on User Experience:** Usability, satisfaction
6. **Implementation Effort:** Time, resources, complexity
7. **Risk:** Probability and severity of negative outcomes

**Total Score = Sum(Impact scores) - Effort - Risk**

## 5. Implementation Procedures

### 5.1 Improvement Proposal Process

1. **Identification:** Anyone can submit an improvement proposal
2. **Documentation:** Use improvement proposal template
3. **Review:** Technical review within 1 week
4. **Approval:** Project owner approval for P0-P2 items
5. **Planning:** Add to sprint backlog with estimated effort
6. **Implementation:** Follow standard development workflow
7. **Validation:** Testing and validation before deployment

### 5.2 Testing and Validation

All improvements must pass:

- [ ] Unit tests (100% coverage of new code)
- [ ] Integration tests
- [ ] Performance benchmarks (no regression)
- [ ] Fairness metrics (no bias increase)
- [ ] Security scans (no new vulnerabilities)
- [ ] Compliance checks (all passing)
- [ ] User acceptance testing (when applicable)

### 5.3 Deployment

- **Development:** Immediate deployment for testing
- **Staging:** Deploy after all tests pass
- **Production:**
  - Canary deployment (5% traffic)
  - Monitor for 24 hours
  - Gradual rollout to 100%
  - Rollback plan ready

## 6. Monitoring and Measurement

### 6.1 Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

| KPI | Target | Measurement |
|-----|--------|-------------|
| Model Accuracy | ≥ 95% | Daily automated |
| P95 Latency | < 250ms | Real-time monitoring |
| Error Rate | < 0.1% | Daily automated |
| Fairness Metrics | Within ±0.1 | Weekly automated |
| Security Incidents | 0 critical | Real-time alerts |
| Compliance Score | 100% | Daily automated |
| User Satisfaction (NPS) | ≥ 50 | Quarterly survey |
| Time to Resolution | < 24h (critical) | Ticket tracking |

